{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, I checked printer BL-PR-FL1 and it is online and healthy, so the problem is on your laptop's print queue rather than the printer. Please try these steps: open Settings, then Bluetooth & devices, then Printers & scanners. Select BL-PR-FL1, choose Open print queue, and cancel all the documents waiting there. Then restart your laptop, which restarts the print spooler. After it restarts, print a test page to BL-PR-FL1. If the test page still doesn't come out, remove the printer and add it back: Add device, or Add manually with the hostname BL-PR-FL1. Let us know if it still fails after that and we'll take another look.",
  "internal_note": "Sender Aisha Khan (user_id 5, HR Generalist, America/New_York, usual hours 09:00-17:00), account active, not locked, no failed logins, VPN enabled, device BL-LT-0105. Checked printer BL-PR-FL1 with check_device_status: online true, firmware 4.2, no warnings, last check-in 2026-10-11 03:08 UTC. Printer is fine, so this is a laptop-side stuck queue per KB-023. Gave the user the KB-023 fix steps (cancel jobs, restart for spooler, test page) and KB-024 re-add as fallback. No action tools were needed. Did not check BL-LT-0105 status or the user's sign-in logs since this does not look like an account issue. Escalate to Tier 2 if the jobs stick again for several users after a restart. Confidence high that the printer is not the cause; the fix is not yet confirmed by the user.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-023",
    "KB-024"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
